        "body": "Snowflake, founded in 2012 and headquartered in Bozeman, MT, describes itself as an AI Data Cloud platform designed to eliminate data silos and support AI, data engineering, applications, and analytics at scale. The company's site presents it as a unified environment for ingesting, processing, analyzing, and modeling data, as well as building and sharing data and AI applications. Customers cited on the site include Under Armour, Booking.com, and Landing AI. Snowflake also describes a Snowflake Postgres offering that brings a relational database environment into its cloud platform without requiring separate data pipelines.\n\nOn the AI product side, Snowflake offers two tracked offerings. Snowflake Arctic is an enterprise-focused large language model released under the Apache 2.0 license with integration into the company's data cloud for commercial use. Snowflake Cortex is a native AI layer within the data cloud that provides LLM functions, vector search, and data residency controls, with governance managed through a framework called Snowflake Horizon.\n\nSnowflake is a publicly traded company on the ticker SNOW, with a CIK of 0001640147. Its most recently reported annual revenue, from a 10-K filing for the period ending January 31, 2026, was $4,683,946,000.",
